# Collected pallet photos are binary and never diffable. Store them with Git LFS
# so a `git clone` does not have to drag every revision of every JPEG.
#
# One-time setup, per machine that will commit photos:
#     git lfs install
#
# See detector-service/dataset/raw/README.md for the storage-budget tradeoff —
# GitHub's free LFS tier is 1 GB, which is roughly 200 pallets at 7 photos each.
detector-service/dataset/raw/**/*.jpg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
detector-service/dataset/raw/**/*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
detector-service/dataset/raw/**/*.png  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
